{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the names of the children of Israel.</b> Notarikon of the initial letters: <b>ו</b>אדם <b>א</b>שר <b>ל</b>ומד <b>ה</b>סדר — a person who studies the order; <b>ש</b>נים <b>מ</b>קרא <b>ו</b>אחד <b>ת</b>רגום — twice Scripture and once translation; <b>ב</b>קול <b>נ</b>עים <b>י</b>שיר <b>י</b>חיה <b>ש</b>נים <b>ר</b>בות <b>א</b>רוכים <b>ל</b>עולם — with a pleasant voice, sings, lives long years, abundant and enduring forever." "<b>And these are the names of the children of Israel, the ones coming</b> — notarikon of the initial letters: שביה — in exile. Even in exile the names of the children of Israel they did not change their names, for because of four things they were redeemed from Egypt: because they did not change their names, etc. And likewise, ואלה — the vav adds to the preceding matter: וימת יוסף ואלה שמות — Joseph commanded them not to change their names, and said to them: even though he changed my name to צפנת פענח, you must not change your names." "<b>את יעקב איש</b> — the masoretic letters form ס\"ת (shabbat): to teach you that because of Shabbat and circumcision, which they observed in Egypt, they were redeemed. The verse begins with vav and ends with vav, corresponding to the twelve tribes. Parable: to one building a palace with one pillar — it fell; he rebuilt with two pillars — it fell; with three — it fell. What did he do? He built it with twelve pillars and it stood. So too Abraham and Isaac — refuse issued from them, until the twelve tribes in whom there was no refuse. And this is the meaning of the vavs of the pillars, for they are the pillars of the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:41.916735904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}